----------------------------------------------------------------------
Origin and attribution
----------------------------------------------------------------------

DocFacts was written inside a private fork of:

    Conway-Research/automaton
    https://github.com/Conway-Research/automaton
    MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Conway

**No code from that project is included in this package.** The four source
modules distributed here were written from scratch for DocFacts:

    spec.ts       feature taxonomy and extraction
    infer.ts      inferring a reference document's interface
    check.ts      comparing a draft against a reference
    docverify.ts  the command-line interface

Each was introduced by a commit authored by this project's author, and
`git log --follow --find-copies-harder` shows no rename, copy or derivation
from any upstream file. No upstream module is imported: the only imports are
Node's own `node:fs` and `node:path`, plus the four files above importing one
another.

This notice records that relationship anyway. The code is independent; the
project it grew up in is not this one, and saying so costs nothing and is the
honest thing to do.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party code and assets
----------------------------------------------------------------------

None.

  - Runtime dependencies:        none
  - Bundled or vendored code:    none
  - Fonts, icons, images:        none (the CLI is text only)
  - Build-time dependency:       TypeScript (Apache-2.0), used to compile
                                 and not distributed in this package

The published archive contains four compiled JavaScript files, four type
declaration files, and documentation. It carries no third-party code, so no
third-party notice is required.
